/* book: lead: In an ideal solution each component's partial pressure is its liquid mole fraction times its own vapour pressure: yiP = xiPisat. That is Raoult's law. Most real pairs, such as ethanol–water, disobey it, so one correction per component is added, the activity coefficient γi. The modified form yiP = xiγiPisat is the working equation behind distillation and flash-drum design. */
